-- title:
--   An idempotent three-torsion projection transports arcs
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. Write $S_+=\{a,a+d,a+d+h\}$, $S_-=\{a,a-d,a-d+h\}$ and $A_\pm(x,y)=1$ if $y-x\in S_\pm$, and zero otherwise. Let $p:G\to G$ be additive, satisfy $p^2=p$ and $3p(x)=0$ for all $x$, and satisfy $p(a)=p(h)=0$, $p(d)=-2d$. Set $f(x)=x+p(x)$. For any $x,y\in G$,
--
--   $$y-x\in S_+\iff f(y)-f(x)\in S_-.$$
--
--   This identifies the explicit additive reflection as a directed graph isomorphism.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourAbelian.lean#L386-L421, lines 386–421; source file SHA-256 c9643d6e3a677d5a903623825d50a309d87175a21ace2b7ab56939d9189f13b1; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianThreeReflection_arc_iff

